WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.429
<i>Legend goes that somewhere
beneath these mountains lies</i>

2
00:00:40.437 --> 00:00:44.582
<i>a gateway between heaven and hell.</i>

3
00:00:45.818 --> 00:00:49.792
<i>It is said that a sacred sisterhood
guards this portal,</i>

4
00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:55.069
<i>and the power of their prayers keeps
the damned from tormenting the living.</i>

5
00:00:56.664 --> 00:00:59.422
<i>Trouble with the damned is...</i>

6
00:00:59.447 --> 00:01:01.628
<i>They never stay put.</i>

7
00:03:45.956 --> 00:03:48.150
<i>My son!</i>

8
00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:51.291
<i>We'll make a man of him, hey, Red?</i>

9
00:03:57.605 --> 00:03:59.377
<i>What's wrong with ya?</i>

10
00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:02.214
<i>Be a man!</i>

11
00:06:24.011 --> 00:06:26.109
Good to see you again.

12
00:06:27.985 --> 00:06:30.576
Where is he?

13
00:06:30.967 --> 00:06:33.831
Boss is careful where he goes.

14
00:06:35.176 --> 00:06:37.045
We've had a little trouble.

15
00:06:37.789 --> 00:06:40.874
Why so many horses?

16
00:06:47.812 --> 00:06:50.719
Boss sent Red and me...

17
00:06:50.744 --> 00:06:52.665
Now, there's just me.

18
00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.597
Like I've said,
we've had a little trouble.

19
00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.927
You brought two too many.

20
00:07:06.819 --> 00:07:08.766
I didn't bring that one.

21
00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:05.154
Do you remember me?

22
00:09:12.971 --> 00:09:14.722
Where is he?

23
00:09:15.761 --> 00:09:17.537
He did not come.

24
00:09:33.547 --> 00:09:35.900
Still, he eludes you.

25
00:09:42.245 --> 00:09:44.407
<i>God's not gonna save ya!</i>

26
00:09:50.248 --> 00:09:53.193
I was to meet him here.

27
00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.589
I have nothing but...

28
00:10:21.611 --> 00:10:25.830
<i>Most times,
when you bring a man to justice,</i>

29
00:10:26.049 --> 00:10:30.312
<i>the axe swings,
the noose tightens,</i>

30
00:10:30.524 --> 00:10:32.314
<i>that's it.</i>

31
00:10:32.409 --> 00:10:35.952
<i>Out here, they come back.</i>

32
00:10:36.399 --> 00:10:39.573
<i>Harder to kill.</i>

33
00:10:40.324 --> 00:10:44.684
<i>The way I finish them?
Rip out their heads.</i>

34
00:10:44.709 --> 00:10:46.500
<i>As for these men?</i>

35
00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.806
<i>Target practice.</i>

36
00:11:38.978 --> 00:11:45.343
Might I say that,
among my many miracles and holy relics,

37
00:11:45.883 --> 00:11:49.517
I do carry certain apothecary goods.

38
00:11:50.737 --> 00:11:56.773
In these forbidding parts,
I sense a woman is a rarity.

39
00:11:58.478 --> 00:12:01.246
Which means a man must improvise.

40
00:12:09.326 --> 00:12:12.152
What piece of you can I buy for a dollar?

41
00:12:12.879 --> 00:12:14.780
My pity.

42
00:12:15.527 --> 00:12:17.547
I was being kind.

43
00:12:17.572 --> 00:12:22.035
I like my men...
heartless.

44
00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:24.151
Get back to your post.

45
00:12:36.947 --> 00:12:38.257
Well?

46
00:12:39.491 --> 00:12:43.305
- That was clever.
- Fancy bitch!

47
00:12:46.182 --> 00:12:47.774
You a thief?

48
00:12:57.689 --> 00:13:01.580
- You don't look like a thief.
- I'm a dancer.

49
00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:06.139
So, where'd you learn a trick like that?

50
00:13:08.085 --> 00:13:09.997
Ballet school.

51
00:13:14.302 --> 00:13:18.204
You know if you cross his path again,
he's liable to kill you.

52
00:13:18.705 --> 00:13:22.431
Death ain't the worst thing
that can happen to you.

53
00:13:24.518 --> 00:13:27.623
You ever heard of "The Gallowwalkers"?

54
00:13:45.951 --> 00:13:50.469
This special tonic will cure all ailments,

55
00:13:50.494 --> 00:13:54.186
and keep the Undead at bay.

56
00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:59.661
Dang priest! Alright,
the wagon's here. Get 'em all up!

57
00:13:59.686 --> 00:14:02.406
- Move! Come on! Get in line!
- Get up!

58
00:14:02.695 --> 00:14:05.073
- Move it!
- Come on!

59
00:14:05.098 --> 00:14:08.017
- Move! Get up!
- Come on, you piece of shit!

60
00:14:08.042 --> 00:14:10.832
Come on, move your ass!
Come on, get in here!

61
00:15:55.334 --> 00:15:59.363
What's a girl gotta do
to get rescued around here?

62
00:16:43.688 --> 00:16:46.178
You that good,
or was that a lucky shot?
62b

63
00:16:46.388 --> 00:16:47.978
Lucky for you.

64
00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:54.138
- So now I owe you?
- Now you owe me.

65
00:17:00.361 --> 00:17:02.186
You got a job in mind?

66
00:17:02.562 --> 00:17:04.165
Yes.

67
00:17:08.755 --> 00:17:10.433
Sir?

68
00:17:11.778 --> 00:17:13.909
Do you know where we are about?

69
00:17:14.933 --> 00:17:16.782
"Enoch's Hammer".

70
00:17:17.252 --> 00:17:20.232
It sounds like a church tower,
a place of tolerance.

71
00:17:20.257 --> 00:17:23.170
They will look kindly
on one of their own. Yeah?

72
00:17:24.608 --> 00:17:27.876
So cruelly treated,
so manifestly wronged!

73
00:17:27.924 --> 00:17:29.769
Do you know this place?

74
00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:34.629
I have family there.
Seven brothers and sisters.

75
00:17:35.833 --> 00:17:38.118
All in the same grave.

76
00:18:01.642 --> 00:18:04.535
Whoa... Whoa there!

77
00:18:15.794 --> 00:18:19.621
Brothers and sisters
of Enoch's Hammer!

78
00:18:20.012 --> 00:18:22.688
Eternally pure of heart.

79
00:18:23.072 --> 00:18:28.695
We have gathered here to
bear witness to God's justice,

80
00:18:28.712 --> 00:18:30.546
on the wicked and the damned.

81
00:18:32.211 --> 00:18:38.740
Bow now your golden heads
and pray for their souls.

82
00:18:41.119 --> 00:18:43.740
- Come on!
- Get down!

83
00:18:43.765 --> 00:18:46.152
- Come on!
- Move!

84
00:18:46.177 --> 00:18:48.986
- Get!
- Get up before I git you some!

85
00:18:53.767 --> 00:18:57.463
Come on, little darlin, get up!
Get up!

86
00:19:09.999 --> 00:19:12.347
Welcome, pilgrims!

87
00:19:14.411 --> 00:19:17.213
I do not call you "prisoners".

88
00:19:18.019 --> 00:19:21.062
Nor do I call these "gallows".

89
00:19:21.602 --> 00:19:25.993
These are the gates
of your salvation.

90
00:19:28.275 --> 00:19:30.607
For this sacrifice...

91
00:19:30.835 --> 00:19:34.343
God has chosen you...

92
00:19:34.454 --> 00:19:36.229
as the lamb.

93
00:19:36.488 --> 00:19:39.019
Just as he chose me...

94
00:19:39.207 --> 00:19:44.557
to help these righteous people
spread justice across the land.

95
00:19:47.347 --> 00:19:51.241
- I was once a sinner...
- Damn right, you were!

96
00:19:51.242 --> 00:19:53.045
Cherry Gaza.

97
00:19:53.327 --> 00:19:57.983
- Y'all virgin eater!
- You whore of Babylon!

98
00:19:58.492 --> 00:20:00.202
You painted cat!

99
00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:02.389
You womb of vipers!

100
00:20:02.835 --> 00:20:06.912
The smell of Jezebel
has no power over me now!

101
00:20:08.202 --> 00:20:14.292
When I saw the devil
rise up from his grave...

102
00:20:15.333 --> 00:20:18.102
Sir, to whom do we plead our case?

103
00:20:18.127 --> 00:20:22.184
- St. Peter!
- You can not hang us without a trial!

104
00:20:23.396 --> 00:20:26.965
I can and I will!

105
00:20:28.154 --> 00:20:33.767
You've already been judged
and found wanting in the eyes of the Lord.

106
00:20:34.158 --> 00:20:38.095
It's through His mercy that he
brought you here to be cleansed, by the rope.

107
00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:41.543
Just as he cleansed me
when I saw the devil!

108
00:20:41.568 --> 00:20:44.135
Rise from the gutter!

109
00:20:46.815 --> 00:20:49.057
I'll be needin' a shirt.

110
00:20:51.026 --> 00:20:53.182
We've only got one color, sir.

111
00:21:10.385 --> 00:21:12.796
You can't go wrong with white.

112
00:21:15.917 --> 00:21:19.551
I'll do my best, sir.
We keep more out the back.

113
00:21:30.656 --> 00:21:35.068
Kiss Cut.
And you must be...?

114
00:22:18.431 --> 00:22:21.858
What do ya' think?
Is it me?

115
00:22:41.649 --> 00:22:45.139
- How many?
- Five.

116
00:23:26.818 --> 00:23:29.161
Alright, stranger.

117
00:23:29.897 --> 00:23:32.643
I'm gonna have to see your face.

118
00:24:32.948 --> 00:24:35.235
The cuffs are a little long.

119
00:24:43.741 --> 00:24:45.335
Bring 'em in.

120
00:25:04.957 --> 00:25:07.611
"And hell came forth
with chains and whips"

121
00:25:07.636 --> 00:25:09.476
"The Horseman of the Apocalypse".

122
00:26:31.351 --> 00:26:34.654
I'm not takin' another step
until you give me some answers.

123
00:26:58.144 --> 00:26:59.773
I'm standin' right here.

124
00:27:04.431 --> 00:27:07.262
You see this?
My fuckin' hands hurt.

125
00:27:42.237 --> 00:27:44.026
Put ​​it on.

126
00:29:54.345 --> 00:29:56.521
Can you do it with your left?

127
00:31:40.631 --> 00:31:42.352
Half now,

128
00:31:43.478 --> 00:31:45.393
half when you finish the job.

129
00:31:46.112 --> 00:31:47.780
How many more?

130
00:31:48.648 --> 00:31:50.756
It doesn't matter.

131
00:31:50.913 --> 00:31:53.485
Only matters if it's
too many for you.

132
00:31:54.533 --> 00:31:57.570
You gonna give me some
answers about those things?

133
00:32:00.821 --> 00:32:03.209
Now that's startin' the story...

134
00:32:03.593 --> 00:32:05.411
at the end.

135
00:32:06.896 --> 00:32:08.989
It begins with a whore.

136
00:32:10.576 --> 00:32:15.510
She's with child when the mines dry up,
so she becomes a thief.

137
00:32:15.527 --> 00:32:17.746
But not very good.

138
00:32:18.287 --> 00:32:22.675
She's headed for the gallows
when Sisters of San Diablo find her.

139
00:32:22.972 --> 00:32:28.685
They take her in and teach her the secrets
of the dead.

140
00:32:29.733 --> 00:32:34.934
When the boy child is born they tell her:
"You must give him up."

141
00:32:35.146 --> 00:32:38.856
"The Gateway to Hell
is no place to raise a child."

142
00:32:39.865 --> 00:32:42.036
So she sends him to an orphanage.

143
00:32:42.281 --> 00:32:47.460
And there... he grows.
And grows...

144
00:32:47.485 --> 00:32:49.755
and grows...

145
00:32:49.780 --> 00:32:52.324
Until the clock strikes twelve.

146
00:32:52.841 --> 00:32:57.350
And then they tell him:
"You're a man. You must leave."

147
00:32:57.852 --> 00:32:59.706
But where...?

148
00:33:01.770 --> 00:33:04.547
A widowed woman meets him,

149
00:33:04.627 --> 00:33:07.842
likes him, takes him in.

150
00:33:09.655 --> 00:33:12.398
She is the mistress
of a slaughter house.

151
00:33:12.516 --> 00:33:15.480
She teaches him a trade,
puts food on the table.

152
00:33:15.505 --> 00:33:17.669
Loves him.

153
00:33:18.514 --> 00:33:20.919
And raises him with...

154
00:33:21.357 --> 00:33:23.754
her daughter.

155
00:33:25.215 --> 00:33:28.986
A beautiful daughter.

156
00:33:29.785 --> 00:33:33.115
He ​​grows to love the daughter.

157
00:33:40.796 --> 00:33:44.405
She is his to protect.

158
00:33:44.633 --> 00:33:49.873
One sunrise, she tells him:
Go with mother to sell the skins.

159
00:33:49.898 --> 00:33:53.911
"Don't worry,
I can take care of myself".

160
00:33:56.466 --> 00:33:58.258
He leaves her.

161
00:33:59.845 --> 00:34:02.170
Five men ride by...

162
00:34:02.499 --> 00:34:04.277
They find her alone...

163
00:34:04.316 --> 00:34:06.019
<i>Go on!</i>

164
00:34:08.254 --> 00:34:10.366
And they make use of her.

165
00:34:16.952 --> 00:34:19.905
<i>You bitch!</i>

166
00:34:22.805 --> 00:34:25.734
She keeps it secret
until she can no more.

167
00:34:25.931 --> 00:34:28.392
For now she is with child.

168
00:34:28.682 --> 00:34:32.990
She begs him: Forgive her,
forget what has happened to her.

169
00:34:33.015 --> 00:34:35.215
For the sake of the unborned.

170
00:34:36.466 --> 00:34:40.974
She says the men are gone,
and to her, they mean... nothing.

171
00:34:40.999 --> 00:34:43.237
But not to him.

172
00:34:43.519 --> 00:34:45.181
No...

173
00:34:45.815 --> 00:34:51.127
For one of them
grows inside of her.

174
00:34:54.144 --> 00:34:56.010
Unbearable.

175
00:34:56.964 --> 00:35:00.161
So for a second time, he leaves.

176
00:35:01.193 --> 00:35:05.800
For the next five years,
he remembers nothing...

177
00:35:06.059 --> 00:35:10.581
but the pain of not
being by her side.

178
00:35:11.800 --> 00:35:14.822
He returns to find her dead.

179
00:35:15.463 --> 00:35:20.161
She died giving birth to that...

180
00:35:20.186 --> 00:35:22.270
Child.

181
00:35:24.545 --> 00:35:27.692
They took from him
the thing he loved most.

182
00:35:29.591 --> 00:35:32.292
Those who were responsible...

183
00:35:35.168 --> 00:35:36.988
would pay.

184
00:37:00.031 --> 00:37:01.394
Troy?

185
00:37:02.534 --> 00:37:03.949
Son!

186
00:37:06.231 --> 00:37:10.403
Get ready!
The boys are sendin' someone!

187
00:37:13.169 --> 00:37:15.229
We're gettin' out of here!

188
00:37:20.643 --> 00:37:23.052
He's here, my darling.

189
00:37:41.348 --> 00:37:43.470
I always hated that bitch!

190
00:37:50.839 --> 00:37:52.689
Please señor! Amigo!

191
00:37:57.001 --> 00:37:58.541
Come on, get us out!

192
00:37:59.557 --> 00:38:01.464
Get us outta here!

193
00:38:12.695 --> 00:38:14.243
Who are you?

194
00:38:20.220 --> 00:38:21.902
Her name...

195
00:38:22.653 --> 00:38:24.419
was Sueno.

196
00:39:20.950 --> 00:39:23.745
- You're late.
- Well...

197
00:39:27.445 --> 00:39:30.499
There was some that needed convincing...

198
00:39:31.008 --> 00:39:32.921
this was a good idea.

199
00:39:36.063 --> 00:39:39.128
A bottle of beer is "a good idea".

200
00:39:39.148 --> 00:39:42.470
Wearing a hat in the rain is "a good idea".

201
00:39:42.487 --> 00:39:45.715
This... is genius.

202
00:40:00.663 --> 00:40:03.039
Shut the hell up, bitch!

203
00:40:13.438 --> 00:40:16.114
You touch me and you're dead!

204
00:40:16.888 --> 00:40:21.002
Compelling argument.
You must be a lawyer.

205
00:40:21.487 --> 00:40:23.368
She's a whore.

206
00:40:24.049 --> 00:40:27.572
An easy mistake.
I apologize.

207
00:40:52.390 --> 00:40:54.310
Good texture.

208
00:40:56.776 --> 00:40:59.723
Tough, yet soft.

209
00:41:13.537 --> 00:41:15.099
You'll fit in well.

210
00:41:20.932 --> 00:41:23.419
I'm looking for the right girl...

211
00:41:24.357 --> 00:41:26.229
for my boy.

212
00:41:40.929 --> 00:41:42.734
You freak!

213
00:41:44.320 --> 00:41:46.123
I get that a lot.

214
00:41:48.429 --> 00:41:51.331
It doesn't stop it hurting though.

215
00:41:55.902 --> 00:41:57.763
God have mercy!

216
00:42:16.810 --> 00:42:20.294
We die, we come back.

217
00:42:20.561 --> 00:42:25.681
You call us...
Gallowwalkers.

218
00:42:31.878 --> 00:42:36.823
Well, if it's good enough for Jesus,
it should be good enough for us.

219
00:42:50.066 --> 00:42:52.709
It's a God damn miracle, ain't it?

220
00:42:52.734 --> 00:42:58.670
It happens, but no one knows
who or how or why.

221
00:42:58.695 --> 00:43:01.057
No one knows.

222
00:43:01.566 --> 00:43:03.298
Here's the thing...

223
00:43:06.401 --> 00:43:08.293
I get shot...

224
00:43:14.763 --> 00:43:17.694
My son, gets shot...

225
00:43:18.586 --> 00:43:21.243
Three of my men get shot.

226
00:43:21.607 --> 00:43:24.700
The son of a bitch even shoots my whore.

227
00:43:28.786 --> 00:43:30.982
I come back.

228
00:43:34.077 --> 00:43:36.877
My men come back.

229
00:43:37.791 --> 00:43:40.425
Even my fucking whore comes back!

230
00:43:40.450 --> 00:43:42.335
But with my son?

231
00:43:42.422 --> 00:43:44.669
Death persists!

232
00:43:49.435 --> 00:43:51.578
Life's little mystery.

233
00:43:59.203 --> 00:44:05.119
Does anyone here know
where I might find the Sisters of San Diablo?

234
00:44:05.503 --> 00:44:07.556
In the Mountain of Resurrection?

235
00:44:11.409 --> 00:44:13.246
No?

236
00:45:11.677 --> 00:45:13.159
Clear!

237
00:46:42.578 --> 00:46:44.423
You sleep now.

238
00:46:46.349 --> 00:46:48.107
Eat if you're hungry.

239
00:46:49.381 --> 00:46:51.221
How much time I got?

240
00:46:51.925 --> 00:46:54.274
Sleep? To eat?

241
00:46:54.339 --> 00:46:55.906
Or to live?

242
00:47:32.198 --> 00:47:33.814
Who is he?

243
00:47:35.697 --> 00:47:37.941
The first I could find.

244
00:47:38.879 --> 00:47:40.429
What happened?

245
00:47:43.204 --> 00:47:45.069
They know who I am.

246
00:47:50.492 --> 00:47:52.431
So now they will come.

247
00:47:53.511 --> 00:47:57.253
You bring this boy because you
think I can not fight at your side?

248
00:48:02.003 --> 00:48:05.407
I can fight.
You know I can fight!

249
00:48:18.961 --> 00:48:21.150
Did one see your face?

250
00:48:24.292 --> 00:48:26.481
It was a mistake.

251
00:48:30.084 --> 00:48:32.343
You don't make mistakes.

252
00:48:33.781 --> 00:48:36.015
Perhaps you want him to come.

253
00:48:37.610 --> 00:48:40.369
Perhaps you want him
to know who hunts him.

254
00:48:41.729 --> 00:48:43.915
You want him to come.

255
00:48:44.995 --> 00:48:48.230
To finish it here,
where it all began.

256
00:49:28.044 --> 00:49:30.080
You gotta shave?

257
00:49:36.916 --> 00:49:40.374
- I got no beard.
- Me neither.

258
00:49:40.563 --> 00:49:42.685
Wanna play a game?

259
00:49:43.342 --> 00:49:47.334
- No, I don't.
- Wanna throw shots for money?

260
00:49:51.858 --> 00:49:53.429
Yes, I do.

261
00:50:39.607 --> 00:50:41.239
My turn.

262
